[version]
1.4.0
[date]
2026-10-21
[whatsnew]
- NEW: Unified GUI Desktop Environment (de/gui.lua)
  - Replaces the tty/gnome/plasma/xfce quartet with one modern DE
  - Top menu bar: ArchOS menu, Apps menu, System menu, Clock
  - Desktop icons (auto-generated from /etc/apps.conf)
  - Clickable windows with title bars, close button, drag support
  - Right-click context menu (via Apps menu)
  - F1 = Run dialog (KRunner-like, type command name to launch)
  - Whole event loop wrapped in pcall (no crashes on bugs)
  - Now the DEFAULT desktop environment for new installs
- NEW: /etc/apps.conf - config file for app list
  - Format: name|path|icon|color (one app per line)
  - To add a new app, just append a line - no code changes needed!
  - To remove an app, delete its line
  - Comments start with #
- FIXED: Editor and other apps not getting CLI arguments
  - Kernel.exec was setting local `arg` instead of _G.arg
  - Files that do `args = arg or {}` at top level now work
- FIXED: pinestore search/install
  - Correct API endpoints: /api/projects/search, /api/project/<id>
  - Properly parses { success=true, projects=[...] } response
  - install now extracts URL from project's install_command field
  - normalizeApp uses real API fields (owner_name, description_short, etc.)
- Installer now defaults to "gui" DE (was "tty")
- Help command updated with gui DE and apps.conf instructions
[/whatsnew]
[files]
de/gui.lua
etc/apps.conf
bin/pinestore.lua
kernel/syscall.lua
bin/help.lua
installer.lua
latest_update.upd
[/files]
